WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.230 --> 00:00:02.370
- Some of you will be surprised to learn

00:00:02.370 --> 00:00:07.033
that one of the hottest
products out there is slime.

00:00:08.020 --> 00:00:09.877
Yeah, kids love to play with it.

00:00:09.877 --> 00:00:11.650
And I am telling you because

00:00:11.650 --> 00:00:15.210
it's in every single one of
the fibers of my carpets,

00:00:15.210 --> 00:00:16.970
it's all over my house

00:00:16.970 --> 00:00:19.790
and the thing that's
really interesting though,

00:00:19.790 --> 00:00:21.870
about slime is it is an art

00:00:21.870 --> 00:00:24.150
and there's a lot of social media on it.

00:00:24.150 --> 00:00:25.370
A ton of tutorials.

00:00:25.370 --> 00:00:28.370
This is like a real thing
and a movement out there.

00:00:28.370 --> 00:00:29.970
And there's actually a really interesting

00:00:29.970 --> 00:00:31.490
soothing aspect to it.

00:00:31.490 --> 00:00:33.300
And when my teachers were telling me like,

00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:35.760
please don't let your daughter
bring stuff in her backpack

00:00:35.760 --> 00:00:37.400
with like squishies and slime,

00:00:37.400 --> 00:00:39.050
it's very sensorial.

00:00:39.050 --> 00:00:41.300
And so it's very soothing
to a lot of people.

00:00:41.300 --> 00:00:44.680
And today we have a slime
expert to tell us more.

00:00:44.680 --> 00:00:46.950
She's actually an amazing entrepreneur too

00:00:47.851 --> 00:00:50.680
and I really, really love her story.

00:00:50.680 --> 00:00:55.680
So please welcome teen slime
entrepreneur, Jay Kang.

00:00:56.700 --> 00:00:57.803
Hi Jay.

00:00:59.053 --> 00:01:01.760
- Hi Drew having me on the show.

00:01:01.760 --> 00:01:03.870
- You know, we've actually
been really excited

00:01:03.870 --> 00:01:05.690
about the prospect of you coming here

00:01:05.690 --> 00:01:07.880
because you launched Snoop Slimes

00:01:07.880 --> 00:01:11.010
when you were just 13 years old.

00:01:11.010 --> 00:01:11.843
How?

00:01:12.780 --> 00:01:15.010
- Well, ever since I was six years old,

00:01:15.010 --> 00:01:16.860
I wanted to become an entrepreneur

00:01:16.860 --> 00:01:18.840
and I would always write down on my,

00:01:18.840 --> 00:01:19.720
you know, dream journal,

00:01:19.720 --> 00:01:22.440
that I always wanted to
you know, own a business,

00:01:22.440 --> 00:01:24.740
but I just never knew
when that time would come.

00:01:24.740 --> 00:01:27.050
But you know, in the summer of 2016,

00:01:27.050 --> 00:01:28.760
I was just scrolling through Instagram,

00:01:28.760 --> 00:01:29.950
like a normal teenager.

00:01:29.950 --> 00:01:32.580
And I found out that, you know,

00:01:32.580 --> 00:01:35.010
these people are playing
with this stuff called slime.

00:01:35.010 --> 00:01:36.950
And at first I didn't
really know much about it.

00:01:36.950 --> 00:01:39.500
So I decided to do more
digging and research into it

00:01:39.500 --> 00:01:41.740
and realized that people are
actually selling this product.

00:01:41.740 --> 00:01:43.510
So I decided to ask my mom,

00:01:43.510 --> 00:01:46.130
if she could help me invest
$200 into this business

00:01:46.130 --> 00:01:47.440
that I want to start.

00:01:47.440 --> 00:01:49.470
And, you know, in the beginning,

00:01:49.470 --> 00:01:50.303
my sister was like, you know,

00:01:50.303 --> 00:01:53.270
you can just get a fancy dinner
with those $200, you know.

00:01:53.270 --> 00:01:56.040
But I decided to use those money

00:01:56.040 --> 00:01:57.890
and invest it into the ingredients

00:01:57.890 --> 00:01:59.710
that I needed to make my first slime.

00:01:59.710 --> 00:02:01.180
And after that,

00:02:01.180 --> 00:02:03.450
I opened my first Etsy shop.

00:02:03.450 --> 00:02:05.760
I started my slime account on Instagram

00:02:05.760 --> 00:02:08.650
and after two weeks I
started getting some sales

00:02:08.650 --> 00:02:09.910
and it just blew up from there.

00:02:09.910 --> 00:02:11.470
- I mean you have

00:02:11.470 --> 00:02:16.470
a full on slime office
with four employees.

00:02:17.190 --> 00:02:18.200
Four.

00:02:18.200 --> 00:02:22.360
How does it feel to be
the CEO of a company?

00:02:22.360 --> 00:02:23.870
- It feels amazing you know,

00:02:23.870 --> 00:02:26.420
being able to have my own
schedule every single day,

00:02:26.420 --> 00:02:27.820
being my own boss.

00:02:27.820 --> 00:02:29.450
It's you know, so amazing

00:02:29.450 --> 00:02:31.990
and also be able to be creative, you know,

00:02:31.990 --> 00:02:33.560
waking up in the morning,

00:02:33.560 --> 00:02:36.120
having to think of new slime ideas

00:02:36.120 --> 00:02:39.230
and just being able to look
at so many different things

00:02:39.230 --> 00:02:41.220
in so many different aspects of business,

00:02:41.220 --> 00:02:42.420
like it's amazing.

00:02:42.420 --> 00:02:43.970
And it's really difficult

00:02:43.970 --> 00:02:45.670
to sometimes balance school, life,

00:02:45.670 --> 00:02:46.670
and business life

00:02:46.670 --> 00:02:48.250
and social life with my friends.

00:02:48.250 --> 00:02:49.660
But with my time management skills,

00:02:49.660 --> 00:02:52.580
I'm able to cope with all
those and work it all out.

00:02:52.580 --> 00:02:56.480
- Well, will you teach me how
to do some slime right now?

00:02:56.480 --> 00:03:01.370
I mean, by the way I hope
my daughters are, you know,

00:03:01.370 --> 00:03:02.950
so savvy like you,

00:03:02.950 --> 00:03:05.340
I'm going to love them
obviously, no matter what.

00:03:05.340 --> 00:03:07.800
And I'm so excited to see, you know,

00:03:07.800 --> 00:03:09.210
like my daughters already think

00:03:09.210 --> 00:03:10.280
they know what they want to do

00:03:10.280 --> 00:03:12.270
and maybe those dreams will stick,

00:03:12.270 --> 00:03:14.430
but I love supporting them.

00:03:14.430 --> 00:03:17.620
And it's funny because as
an adult slime is like,

00:03:17.620 --> 00:03:19.450
it really gets messy in your house

00:03:19.450 --> 00:03:20.870
when your kids are working with it

00:03:20.870 --> 00:03:22.510
and I've always supported them.

00:03:22.510 --> 00:03:23.660
I'm like play with the slime,

00:03:23.660 --> 00:03:24.493
I'll figure it out,

00:03:24.493 --> 00:03:25.326
I'll clean it up.

00:03:25.326 --> 00:03:27.720
Okay so teach me, what did we do?

00:03:27.720 --> 00:03:28.553
- All right Drew.

00:03:28.553 --> 00:03:30.290
So we'll be making a
candy corn inspired slime

00:03:30.290 --> 00:03:32.150
since Halloween is coming up soon.

00:03:32.150 --> 00:03:36.890
So we're first going to pour
two cups of glue into the bowl.

00:03:36.890 --> 00:03:38.051
- By the way,

00:03:38.051 --> 00:03:41.670
I wish as this is what the slime
kit at my house looks like.

00:03:41.670 --> 00:03:44.230
Olive just makes her own ratios,

00:03:44.230 --> 00:03:45.710
it's all over the place.

00:03:45.710 --> 00:03:47.500
I mean, she's like a mad scientist.

00:03:47.500 --> 00:03:49.920
I call her the alchemist arsonist,

00:03:49.920 --> 00:03:52.520
which I know sounds
like a really dark name,

00:03:52.520 --> 00:03:54.400
but she really is.

00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:56.780
She loves to get into everything.

00:03:56.780 --> 00:03:57.980
- Yeah. It's all an experiment.

00:03:57.980 --> 00:03:59.410
All right. Now we're going to add

00:03:59.410 --> 00:04:03.010
one teaspoon of baking
soda into the same bowl.

00:04:03.010 --> 00:04:03.843
- Done.

00:04:03.843 --> 00:04:05.900
- [Jay] We can use a spatula

00:04:05.900 --> 00:04:08.900
and we're going to mix both of
these ingredients up together

00:04:10.300 --> 00:04:11.650
and just mix it thoroughly

00:04:11.650 --> 00:04:15.100
you got to make sure
everything's just all mixed.

00:04:15.100 --> 00:04:15.933
- Oh my God.

00:04:15.933 --> 00:04:18.663
Literally I am in Olive's
happy place right now.

00:04:20.010 --> 00:04:22.490
If we were playing with
like Barbies and princesses,

00:04:22.490 --> 00:04:24.363
I'd be in Frankie's happy place.

00:04:26.290 --> 00:04:28.030
- All alright now we're going to take some

00:04:28.030 --> 00:04:29.710
contact slime solution.

00:04:29.710 --> 00:04:30.680
- Yup right here.

00:04:30.680 --> 00:04:34.360
- And you're gonna pour
just a little bit at a time

00:04:34.360 --> 00:04:35.193
into the slime.

00:04:35.193 --> 00:04:36.720
You don't want to make it, you know,

00:04:36.720 --> 00:04:38.050
you don't want to pour too much in,

00:04:38.050 --> 00:04:40.240
because it will make the slime too stiff.

00:04:40.240 --> 00:04:41.860
But just keep pouring a little bit.

00:04:41.860 --> 00:04:43.690
Don't pour too much.

00:04:43.690 --> 00:04:45.970
There you go. Yup.

00:04:45.970 --> 00:04:47.370
And then just keep stirring.

00:04:48.240 --> 00:04:49.523
Keep stirring Drew.

00:04:50.610 --> 00:04:53.190
- That's a contact solution.

00:04:53.190 --> 00:04:54.190
Yeah that makes sense.

00:04:54.190 --> 00:04:56.940
I see all these bottles
of like empty OptiFresh

00:04:56.940 --> 00:04:58.030
all over the floor.

00:04:58.030 --> 00:04:59.733
So yeah, that makes sense.

00:05:00.930 --> 00:05:04.410
- Okay. I think we might need
to add a little bit more so

00:05:04.410 --> 00:05:06.040
add little bit more
contact slime solution.

00:05:06.040 --> 00:05:06.913
- Okay.

00:05:07.750 --> 00:05:10.975
- You want the slime to
start getting off the bowl,

00:05:10.975 --> 00:05:11.840
start unsticking.

00:05:11.840 --> 00:05:13.680
- Oh, Oh, Oh, okay.

00:05:13.680 --> 00:05:14.950
Oh God.

00:05:14.950 --> 00:05:16.220
- Keep mixing.

00:05:16.220 --> 00:05:17.053
- Okay. You know what?

00:05:17.053 --> 00:05:17.886
By the way,

00:05:19.270 --> 00:05:21.420
I think what we can do also

00:05:21.420 --> 00:05:24.540
is like turn this into a workout.

00:05:24.540 --> 00:05:26.910
I think maybe if you open a gym membership

00:05:26.910 --> 00:05:31.180
to a slime factory and then we can, like,

00:05:31.180 --> 00:05:35.740
the moms can help their kids
by working out their mom arms.

00:05:35.740 --> 00:05:36.573
- That would be perfect.

00:05:36.573 --> 00:05:38.043
All right keep stirring.

00:05:39.010 --> 00:05:40.060
- Oh God.

00:05:40.060 --> 00:05:40.893
- I think you need a little more.

00:05:40.893 --> 00:05:42.950
- You know what, I'm I'm Oh, Oh,

00:05:42.950 --> 00:05:44.210
can I please add these?

00:05:44.210 --> 00:05:45.440
These are my favorite.

00:05:45.440 --> 00:05:47.413
These are my absolute favorite.

00:05:49.210 --> 00:05:51.090
Someone else made this wonderful slime.

00:05:51.090 --> 00:05:53.180
Let's face it, I did not make this.

00:05:53.180 --> 00:05:56.760
But I'm adding the
colored balls in, Oh God.

00:05:56.760 --> 00:05:59.353
Now I'm going rogue, I'm fired.

00:06:00.610 --> 00:06:01.923
- [Jay] Keep adding it.

00:06:01.923 --> 00:06:04.500
- And I've got googly eyes.

00:06:04.500 --> 00:06:06.000
I'm just, I'm going for it.

00:06:06.000 --> 00:06:07.290
Cause we're going to commercial

00:06:07.290 --> 00:06:09.030
and I'm like you know what?

00:06:09.030 --> 00:06:11.543
My slime is getting everything.

00:06:12.690 --> 00:06:14.127
How does this look?

00:06:15.617 --> 00:06:16.679
- That looks amazing.

00:06:16.679 --> 00:06:17.512
- Oh God.

00:06:19.000 --> 00:06:20.743
By the way I'm not kidding.

00:06:21.600 --> 00:06:23.580
If anyone has any interest,

00:06:23.580 --> 00:06:26.880
please go on social media
and get into the slime world

00:06:26.880 --> 00:06:28.820
because it is so relaxing,

00:06:28.820 --> 00:06:30.570
it is so artistic.

00:06:30.570 --> 00:06:34.970
It really is a very important
movement for people.

00:06:34.970 --> 00:06:37.840
And like, it's so nice to meet you.

00:06:37.840 --> 00:06:42.650
And it is so nice to see a
young woman such as yourself,

00:06:42.650 --> 00:06:45.430
doing so much with your
life at such a young age,

00:06:45.430 --> 00:06:47.490
you are such an inspiration.

00:06:47.490 --> 00:06:50.810
And my daughter is going to
be so jealous of this segment

00:06:50.810 --> 00:06:52.930
when she sees that I'm in deep trouble.

00:06:52.930 --> 00:06:55.990
So do you mind if I a sidebar with you Jay

00:06:55.990 --> 00:07:00.920
and maybe see if I could ever
like FaceTime you with her?

00:07:00.920 --> 00:07:04.850
- I would love to send her any
slimes that she would like.

00:07:04.850 --> 00:07:05.683
- Oh my God,

00:07:05.683 --> 00:07:08.100
she'll be your biggest
fan Jay and we are too.

00:07:08.100 --> 00:07:10.539
Thank you so much for coming.

00:07:10.539 --> 00:07:13.122
(upbeat music)

